<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 1264) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: people following your review could land one frame ahead of you.</b> When you paused partway through a frame, Asobi showed that frame but told everyone following (the web page, the iPad and iPhone app, other Macs) the next one. Everyone now stops on the frame you see.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1259) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcases in HEVC:</b> each showcase now also carries an HEVC copy — the same picture in about two thirds of the data, so it streams more smoothly (4K most of all). Browsers and the iPad and iPhone app that play HEVC get it; the rest get H.264 as before.</li>
<li><b>Knowing when H.264 can go:</b> every visit to a showcase records whether the viewer could play HEVC, and the Review Manager counts them, for each showcase and across them all.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1255) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed:</b> sharing a clip whose picture starts a moment after its sound (common in files cut from streams, or exported without an edit list) failed with “Cannot Open”. The first frames now show the clip's first picture, and the share goes through.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1250) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Change who can open a review after posting it:</b> Edit… on a live review in the Review Manager switches between anyone with the link and only the people you've invited (and one browser per person). It works with the review's session closed. The link stays the same.</li>
<li><b>Edit… in the Showcase window</b>, as well as in the Review Manager.</li>
<li><b>Each review and showcase remembers what was changed after posting</b> ("sign-in turned off", "only invited people can open it"), with the date, so the viewing report makes sense.</li>
<li>Sign-ins taken in the iPad app's event mode show as "(at an event)" in a showcase's viewing.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1232) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcases on your iPad or iPhone, no links to type:</b> in the Showcase window, Pair iPad or iPhone… shows a code. Point the device's Camera at it and tap Open in Asobi, and the Asobi app's start screen lists this Mac's live showcases. When you make, edit, extend or end a showcase here, the list follows. The list is sealed with the code's key, so the relay can't read it. Make a New Pairing… shuts out the devices paired before. Also in the Review Manager.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1210) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Edit a showcase after posting it:</b> in the Review Manager, Edit… on a live showcase changes its title, the line under it, sign-in, Skip and the closing card's button and link. The link stays the same, nothing is sent again, and the session doesn't need to be open.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1202) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Reopening a showcase:</b> after a restart, reopening a live showcase from the Review Manager no longer leaves its window waiting on the email preview. The preview comes back, and Save GIF works again.</li>
<li><b>Review Manager:</b> each link now says how long it really works, with or without Asobi open.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1199) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcases in more than one tab:</b> each tab now has its own Share and Showcase windows, so a new tab with a different clip can make its own showcase while another stays live.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
